# The Dockerfile does `COPY . .`, so anything not excluded here is baked into
# the published image.
#
# Two entries from the Wagtail scaffold had to go, because what they excluded
# is now the site itself:
#
#   /static/  the scaffold excluded built assets; static/ is a source
#             directory here and holds the stylesheet the site is built on.
#   parts/    had no leading slash, so it matched content/parts/ and
#             public/images/parts/ alike: all 130 markdown files and all 185
#             media files.
#
# Both were harmless while a database held the content. Neither is now.

# Built on the host, for the host. The image runs its own `uv sync`.
.venv/

.env
.git/
.github/
.gitignore
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Written by collectstatic during the build.
staticfiles/

# Nothing should produce one of these any more; the project has no database.
*.sqlite3
*.sqlite3-wal
*.sqlite3-shm

.DS_Store
*.swp
.vscode/
.idea/
node_modules/
coverage
